{% comment %}
  Theme template body (Liquid runs here). Mirrors shopify/accessibility-statement-page.example.liquid.

  Setup (theme): add this file + templates/page.carbon-accessibility.json to the theme, then
  Pages → Theme template → "carbon-accessibility". Clear the page body. Set page Title to "Accessibility statement"
  (for nav, browser tab, SEO — this section supplies the visible H1 below).

  Setup (no Liquid): use shopify/accessibility-statement-shopify-admin.html — set Title to "Accessibility statement",
  then paste the inner <div> in Show HTML (no second H1 in the paste).

  Widget: point "Accessibility statement URL" at this page, e.g. https://www.shopcarbon.com/pages/accessibility
{% endcomment %}
<div class="page-width rte">
  <h1>Accessibility statement</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: {{ 'now' | date: '%B %e, %Y' }}</em></p>

  <h2>Our commitment</h2>
  <p>
    CARBON is committed to making our website usable for people with disabilities. We strive to align with
    the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 Level AA and to improve our store over time.
  </p>

  <h2>Assistive tools</h2>
  <p>
    Our site includes <strong>Carbon Assist</strong>, an accessibility menu. Use the accessibility icon on the screen
    to adjust text size, contrast, motion, reading tools, and more.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party content</h2>
  <p>
    Some embedded content (videos, maps, checkout or payment experiences from partners) may not be fully controlled by
    us. If something is hard to use, please contact us and we will help or provide an alternative where possible.
  </p>

  <h2>Feedback</h2>
  <p>
    If you experience difficulty accessing any part of our store, contact us at
    <a href="mailto:support@shopcarbon.com">support@shopcarbon.com</a>
    or through our <a href="/pages/contact-us">contact page</a>. We aim to respond within two business days.
  </p>

  <h2>Formal complaints</h2>
  <p>
    If you are not satisfied with our response, you may contact a local disability rights organization or the relevant
    authority in your region.
  </p>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Accessibility statement (Carbon)",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
